//
// loft#1210's CONTROL half. A bare `local += <source>` stays refused, and letting the FIELD
// form through does not let the LOCAL form through with it.
//
// The two places are governed by different rules, which is the whole reason this file exists
// separately from the positive half. A FIELD append is the supported single-element/concat
// site, so `(N-Store)` decides it and says *warn, and the store proceeds*. A LOCAL `+=` is
// refused by @PLAN52's ambiguity rule whatever its source type — `vec<vec<T>> += vec<T>` is
// both "push one element" and "concat", so the bare spelling is rejected and `+= [elem]` is
// required. Nullability has nothing to do with that one.
//
// So this is the cell that says the loft#1210 peel is scoped to the destination it was written
// for. If a build starts COMPILING either function below, the fix has reached past the field
// append into the place-kind next door, where a different rule already has an answer.
//
// In its own file because a firing `@EXPECT_ERROR` stops a file before it runs; the positive
// half is `1210-a-nullable-append-source-warns-and-stores.loft`.
//
// @falsified-at: 54826d97 — MEASURED, and like every control the channel is
//   `check_diagnostics` rather than the exit: both cells report the same diagnostic on the
//   parent commit as on the fixed build, which is the POINT — this is the cell that must NOT
//   move. What makes it falsifiable is the opposite build: with the peel applied to a LOCAL
//   destination as well, both `@EXPECT_ERROR` lines go unmatched and `tests/wrap.rs` fails the
//   file.
//   ⚠ That control is on no public ref, so this receipt records a falsification that
//   cannot be re-run — see TESTING.md § The patch receipt for the form that can be.
//   CHANNEL: `check_diagnostics`, not the exit — as for every control here, both cells report
//   the same diagnostic on the parent commit as on the fixed build, which is the point: this
//   is the cell that must NOT move. It falsifies on the opposite build, with the peel applied
//   to a LOCAL.

// The nullable source — the shape loft#1210 fixed one place-kind over.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot change type from vector<integer>
fn test_1210b_nullable_source_into_a_local_is_refused() {
  s1210b: vector<integer>? = [1, 2];
  d1210b: vector<integer> = [];
  d1210b += s1210b;
  assert(len(d1210b) == 2, "unreached");
}

// The DENSE source beside it, and it is refused by a DIFFERENT message — @PLAN52's ambiguity
// rule, named in as many words. That the two cells are turned away by two different rules is
// the point rather than an untidiness: the nullable one never reaches the ambiguity check
// because the local's type would have to change first, so neither refusal is evidence for the
// other and both are worth pinning.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: vector `+= elem` is ambiguous
fn test_1210b_dense_source_into_a_local_is_refused_too() {
  s1210c: vector<integer> = [1, 2];
  d1210c: vector<integer> = [];
  d1210c += s1210c[0];
  assert(len(d1210c) == 1, "unreached");
}
